    "question": "What SPF sunscreen do I actually need, and does a higher number meaningfully protect me more?",
    "summary": "SPF measures UVB protection on a logarithmic scale, meaning SPF 30 blocks 97% of rays and is sufficient for most people, while very high SPF numbers offer only marginal additional protection. Proper application and reapplication matter far more than choosing the highest SPF available.",
